<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>SPOTLIGHT</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ad3c68a59ff5d62ed1d24129fe4f79635db54b2b3d08b7005ca7597fc4f91f2</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T18:22:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261010-spotlight" /><summary type="html">Adam Barron is an independent Middle East political analyst and consultant, specialising primarily in Yemen, where he has reported from the capital, Sanaa, for The Economist. He writes for Foreign Policy and The Atlantic.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Riyadh airport suspends operations after attack leaves multiple people wounded</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4d058170230e62c4eae35b09edc20a8e93bffc42ae9106c6a89779a0fdd9845</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T18:03:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-riyadh-airport-suspends-operations-after-attack-leaves-multiple-people-wounded" /><summary type="html">Saudi authorities on Saturday said that they had suspended operations at Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport after a new attack there left multiple people wounded. An attack on the airport by the Houthis on Thursday killed three people and damaged a plane, though the Iran-backed group did not announce any new attacks on Saturday.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Convicted murderer Christa Pike leaves hospital, returns to prison after botched execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea8b1444700dab2abb83763a0ccfb8e38034f5d80151aba24d0739aeda2fadb1</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T17:41:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-leaves-hospital-returns-to-prison-after-botched-execution" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike's lawyers on Saturday said that the 50-year-old convicted murderer has been discharged from the hospital and returned to prison. Pike was transported to the hospital in critical condition on September 30 after she survived Tennessee's botched effort to execute her for murdering a classmate when she was a teenager.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Trump lashes out at Zelensky, says Ukraine needs new president who will agree to end war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2c2d68dc3b5a1314ea9f8215da7bb7404b0d53f4befc9ec857263b62af70ba5</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T17:39:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children--2e66a7264c75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children" /></entry><entry><title>India protests: New 'cockroach' movement leader named</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:736d960ee349854060487f14f0217d49c1b2fb4dd08277c92209618008e89f02</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T16:14:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-protests-new-cockroach-movement-leader-named" /><summary type="html">Indian police detained the head of the satirical "cockroach" online movement on Saturday, the group said, ahead of a major protest against the Election Commission that prompted strict security measures.
 
"They seem to have seen that coming," notes France 24's Andrew Hilliar. In a prerecorded video, Abhijeet Dipke, founder of the Cockroach Party, names an interim leader to take over.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa: Anti-migrant unrest flares in Durban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7263cb326f1bc37ab006b1456f1832b649892103f60089400987e80208d712d6</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T16:12:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-south-africa-anti-migrant-unrest-flares-in-durban" /><summary type="html">Police in Durban were battling a fresh wave of anti-migrant unrest. Shops were looted, homes were torched and foreign nationals were targeted as crowds took to the streets for a second day. The violence has revived fears of rising xenophobic tensions over immigration.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Ebola tests negative as contact tracing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec67eeac6e0178fc74e416936fa97a873aae3fc51c7a84b5e674ef725018106</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T16:10:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-kenya-ebola-tests-negative-as-contact-tracing-continues" /><summary type="html">Tests have come back negative for a person suspected of having Ebola who was reportedly in quarantine at a hospital, following rumours circulating over the past 24 hours. Meanwhile, in Nairobi, authorities are racing to trace contacts of Kenya's first Ebola death, reported on Monday. Our correspondent Bastien Renouil tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Abbas postpones Palestinian elections, sets presidential poll for September 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:012b9997136f56f4765e8514cdfd79c570f33e608a5e32a3621c81732bd57c12</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T16:09:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-abbas-postpones-palestinian-elections-sets-presidential-poll-for-september-2027" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas on Saturday postponed legislative elections due next month until September 11, ​2027, and called ‌a presidential poll for the same date, blaming Israel and the security situation in the Palestinian territories for the ⁠delay. Our correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms: "It does look like the Republicans will lose control of the House of Representatives"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8511f68f179e816bf66852cc3b30e47ad3c8866e88ec6f021c7ecda19f4e011</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T16:04:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-midterms-it-does-look-like-the-republicans-will-lose-control-of-the-house-of-representatives" /><summary type="html">Most of the political world is focused on next month's midterm elections in the US. "It does look like the Republicans will lose control of the House of Representatives," says our guest, Bruce Stokes, a visiting senior fellow at the German Marshall Fund of the United States.</summary></entry><entry><title>French cycling prodigy Seixas claims first Monument victory at Giro di Lombardia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1d3a9cd28bfac9fdc7cfba42d18e7bef1d77b3c9f0de39d1b0e513faecf4598</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T15:58:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261010-french-cycling-prodigy-seixas-claims-first-monument-victory-at-giro-di-lombardia" /><summary type="html">French prodigy Paul Seixas claimed his first Monument win at the Giro di Lombardia on Saturday. The victory makes the 20-year-old the fourth-youngest winner of a Monument race.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Russian strikes kill 15, including a young girl</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48d5c11feb0b52c415cf0ee77439e45d75398222aaeb7beda3767dc6f7df5479</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T15:56:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-war-in-ukraine-russian-strikes-kill-15-including-a-young-girl" /><summary type="html">Early Saturday, Russia targeted residential neighbourhoods in the southeastern city of Zaporizhzhia with "five guided aerial bombs", according to Ukraine's National Police.

At least 15 people were killed, including three children, Ukraine's State Emergency Service said. The family of a young girl killed in the attack was inconsolable.</summary></entry><entry><title>India detains thousands, locks down Delhi to foil election chief protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a077110463b52a9aa348204dbee9c68e07045a9c46a8ecaa439f9081ac37bd1a</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T15:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-thousands-locks-down-delhi-to-foil-election-chief-protest" /><summary type="html">Police detained more than 2,000 protesters and the founder of the "cockroach" youth movement in Delhi on Saturday as security forces locked down parts of the capital to thwart a rally demanding the resignation of India's election chief. Our correspondent Navodita Kumari tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Death penalty: Why are executions increasing worldwide?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1834634c90619b988c6e16f9b5e284de2ce37d6ecb1dd71eb9ddd1f9703f50fd</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T15:52:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-death-penalty-why-are-executions-increasing-worldwide" /><summary type="html">October 10 marks the World Day Against the Death Penalty. This week, the EU condemned capital punishment as a cruel and degrading form of punishment. But not all world leaders share this view. We discuss why executions are on the rise with our guest François Picard, host of "Death Row Stories".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian attack on Ukrainian city kills 15, a day after Trump eases diesel sanctions on Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f37ceec9617ea7c4ad42f0b685b3f2536607cc256ab5b9b8fdec321c89005be</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T15:39:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-russian-attack-on-ukrainian-city-kills-15-a-day-after-trump-eases-diesel-sanctions-on-moscow" /><summary type="html">Fifteen people, including three children, were killed in a Russian attack on the southern Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia on Saturday, a day after US President Donald Trump announced a deal to lift sanctions on Russian diesel, in a major setback for Kyiv. Our correspondent Gulliver Cragg tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>India detains 'cockroach' movement leaders in bid to thwart election protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:338a1a4b1e9fcace5101da5bcb1bd961d495113cd92e202c2c1c8e622cd21e17</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T15:37:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-movement-leaders-in-bid-to-thwart-election-protest" /><summary type="html">Indian police detained the head of the satirical "cockroach" online movement on Saturday as hundreds of protesters demanding the election commissioner's resignation gathered in New Delhi despite a heavy security crackdown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lens see off Lyon as Ligue 1 season resumes after international break</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f714853581c3049ebe70994e9bce3261d405f6073d8cdcb38c3411038761421</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T14:10:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261010-lens-see-off-lyon-as-ligue-1-season-resumes-after-international-break" /><summary type="html">Lens put an end to a four-match winless run by beating Lyon 2-1 on Friday night, in what was the first Ligue 1 fixture after a three-week international break. Paris Saint-Germain head coach Luis Enrique has brushed off concerns about Ousmane Dembélé's recent form, having rested the forward for Saturday's match against promoted side Le Mans.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal hits Ronaldo with provisional suspension for walking out on national team</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d16f612cca0c79572e7649581d558f8343d2f9881e2097221f28691ea85eea3</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T14:02:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261010-portugal-hits-ronaldo-with-provisional-suspension-for-walking-out-on-national-team--8ffcbd4fbca1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261010-portugal-hits-ronaldo-with-provisional-suspension-for-walking-out-on-national-team" /><summary type="html">Portuguese Football Federation announced on Saturday that it has provisionally suspended star attacker Cristiano Ronaldo and opened disciplinary proceedings against the 41-year-old over his decision to walk out on the national team last month.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen says advancing against Houthis around key Bab al-Mandab strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca51cebff9f991f04006790a90311886e6f9edb71ccabb1d27c2583ff0fe277e</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:45:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-yemen-says-forces-made-advances-against-houthis-around-key-waterway--4e2af6409b56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-yemen-says-forces-made-advances-against-houthis-around-key-waterway" /><summary type="html">Yemen said Saturday that forces were advancing against the Houthis around the Bab al-Mandab strait, a week after the country's Saudi-backed government announced that it was initiating a counter-offensive to take back territory seized by the pro-Iran group during last month's lightning offensive. In Riyadh, diplomatic sources reported a missile attack on the civilian airport, with at least five Saudi nationals wounded being treated in intensive care.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Zelensky clash over diesel deal as Russian strikes on Ukraine kill 21, including children</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2b69918719cc98ec8b12602183cae6a10ee89cdc756dbe79b4b6ed8f70d6676</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-children" /><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Palestinian president Abbas postpones legislative elections, sets presidential poll for September 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2e9028244ba222321090c3ea6d62ba5ae014df6497a2e278bd932a8191950e1</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T11:58:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027--79eb133759e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027" /></entry><entry><title>Palestinian president Abbas postpones legislative, presidential elections to September 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2c41224cb0706e354d25bde16801b9b0129b5d1d66f2b4a4852ef73fce70a72</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T11:56:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027--79eb133759e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027" /><summary type="html">⁠⁠Palestinian president ​Mahmoud ​Abbas announced on Saturday that legislative ⁠elections would be postponed from November ​28 to September ​11, 2027, the ​official Palestinian news agency ⁠WAFA reported. In his presidential decree, Abbas set the next presidential elections for that day as well.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>October 7 scars push Israel's first-time voters to right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c843c4efe65ba478e76247f62be1d384744d34c85a40b5693c49c5e36eef16d6</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T11:01:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-october-7-scars-push-israel-s-first-time-voters-to-right--a4d681b52038.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-october-7-scars-push-israel-s-first-time-voters-to-right" /><summary type="html">Like hundreds of thousands of Israelis, Amihai will be of voting age for the first time since Hamas carried out its attack on October 7, 2023. When he casts his ballot this month, he has one priority above all -- security.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hunger and malnutrition stalk Gazans, a year on from ceasefire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffbd5346544d4bfe937be232915260ba6d9dec01991dbb13ce6ce10b7b012135</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T11:00:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire--48988060ff3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">Every day, Gazan mother Niyaha al-Masri spends six exhausting hours or more queueing at a community kitchen in the hope of getting some food for her family. It has been a year since a ceasefire between Hamas and Israel was supposed to allow food to flood into the ruined territory, yet widespread hunger persists there.</summary></entry><entry><title>Severe injuries at French student protests draw scrutiny to police tactics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f28fd46b0983e49fb38424535c42b67d9457bf70ffd758cafca4db09e68de2a</id><updated>2026-10-10T20:10:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T10:20:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261010-injuries-french-student-protests-draw-scrutiny-to-police-tactics--364db9c4aa5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261010-injuries-french-student-protests-draw-scrutiny-to-police-tactics" /><summary type="html">Twenty-four investigations have been opened by French police watchdog IGPN into incidents linked to the ongoing high school protest movement, the interior ministry said. The police response has reignited calls to scrap rubber bullets and launcher-fired riot-control weapons, long denounced by rights groups and UN experts as dangerous and excessive.</summary><category term="France" /></entry></feed>
